   "path": "dek.en",
   "before": "Wu Qi held Wei's western frontier at Xihe, and even Tian Wen, chief minister at the time, admitted that his record was the greater. A later chief minister, Gongshu, resented him and wanted to drive him out, so he laid a two-step trap: persuade the ruler to offer Wu Qi a princess in marriage, then bring Wu Qi home to watch Gongshu's own wife, a princess, treat her husband with contempt. Wu Qi declined the marriage, and the ruler grew suspicious and stopped trusting him.",
