   "path": "sections.story.4.en",
   "before": "The servant's plan: in step one, Gongshu would tell Marquis Wu that Wu Qi was a man of worth, but that the marquis's state was small and bordered on mighty Qin, and he privately feared Wu Qi had no mind to stay. In the servant's script, the marquis would ask what to do. Gongshu would then propose testing Wu Qi with the offer of a princess: if he meant to stay he would surely accept, and if not he would surely decline, so the offer would serve as a divination of his intentions. In step two, Gongshu would then invite Wu Qi home and have the princess he had married flare up and slight him in front of Wu Qi. Seeing a princess treat her husband with such contempt, the servant predicted, Wu Qi would surely turn the marriage down.",
   "after": "The servant's plan: in step one, Gongshu would tell Marquis Wu that Wu Qi was a man of worth, but that the marquis's state was small and bordered on mighty Qin, and he privately feared Wu Qi had no mind to stay. In the servant's script, the marquis would ask what to do. Gongshu would then propose testing Wu Qi with the offer of a princess: if he meant to stay he would surely accept, and if not he would surely decline, so the offer would serve as a divination of his intentions. In step two, Gongshu would then invite Wu Qi home and have his own wife, the princess, flare up and slight Gongshu in front of Wu Qi. Seeing a princess treat her husband with such contempt, the servant predicted, Wu Qi would surely turn the marriage down.",
